Fillets: a closed rounding that rolls on an edge (an obstacle, 0011)
starting at that edge's vertex, where the seam of a face around it starts
too (mitcad#239). Example: a disc's bottom edge rounded wider than the
disc's side and the bevel above it, the ball rolling on the bevel's top
edge all round; the disc, bevel and neck made of separate solids, so that
the seams meet at the edge's vertex. The rounding's first point there was
found on the neck's seam, and ChFi3d_FilDS cut that arc at the point as if
the rounding ended on it: the seam went, and the topological build lost
the faces above (an unorientable shape of three faces).

- ChFi3d_FilDS, the first surface data of a stripe: a point at a vertex on
  a side rolling on an obstacle no longer cuts the arc it was found on; the
  obstacle's end at that vertex is handled by CutEdge, as at the last
  surface data's end, which already skipped such points.
